From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen.kooi@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] monza.cfg: add OV5647 camera support, build CAN drivers in

CONFIG_VIDEO_OV5647 is needed to use a Raspberry Pi v1 camera module
on the Monza board.

CONFIG_CAN itself is not selected by this file, so olddefconfig caps
it at =m via defconfig regardless of any submodule's own setting.
Build CONFIG_CAN=y plus the three USB CAN adapter drivers into the
kernel rather than as modules, so they don't depend on that cap.

Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen.kooi@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 recipes-kernel/linux/linux-qcom-next/configs/monza.cfg | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-qcom-next/configs/monza.cfg b/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-qcom-next/configs/monza.cfg
index 5e7f194..16cd390 100644
--- a/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-qcom-next/configs/monza.cfg
+++ b/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-qcom-next/configs/monza.cfg
@@ -20,14 +20,20 @@ CONFIG_SND_SOC_SC8280XP=m
 CONFIG_SND_SOC_SC8280XP=m
 # PCIe M.2 E-key connector power sequencing (WiFi/BT LGA module)
 CONFIG_POWER_SEQUENCING_PCIE_M2=m
+# OmniVision OV5647 sensor support; used in Raspberry Pi v1 camera
+CONFIG_VIDEO_OV5647=m
+# Built-in, not a module: USB CAN adapter drivers below depend on CAN and
+# would otherwise be silently capped at =m by olddefconfig regardless of
+# their own value, since defconfig sets CONFIG_CAN=m.
+CONFIG_CAN=y
 # support for USB CAN adapters for demos and testing
 #
 # this enables popular hardware like CANable, Candlelight and PEAK System
 # PCAN-USB, supported by the slcan, gs_usb and peak_usb drivers respectively

 # Serial / USB serial CAN Adaptors (slcan)
-CONFIG_CAN_SLCAN=m
+CONFIG_CAN_SLCAN=y
 # Geschwister Schneider UG and candleLight compatible interfaces
-CONFIG_CAN_GS_USB=m
+CONFIG_CAN_GS_USB=y
 # PEAK PCAN-USB/USB Pro interfaces for CAN 2.0b/CAN-FD
-CONFIG_CAN_PEAK_USB=m
+CONFIG_CAN_PEAK_USB=y
--
2.34.1
